  "goodToKnow": "Das Vaterland means fatherland, one's native country. The third verse of the Deutschlandlied, the only one sung as the national anthem, begins Einigkeit und Recht und Freiheit für das deutsche Vaterland. Because of its heavy use in nationalist and Nazi propaganda, many Germans today avoid the word and prefer Heimat or simply Deutschland. Speakers of other languages often use the matching word with fewer qualms. Plural: die Vaterländer."
